Initial outputs default zeros; instance state initial values. Could declare outputs with initial? BOOL false, WORD 0, LREAL 0.0. Initial variables: sampleCount maybe INT 0, previousTrigger false. History array [0..99] of LREAL, lastValidWindowSize INT maybe 0 (last valid configured window), write index? sum? Need arithmetic accuracy and behavior.

Semantics:
- Each scan:
  - valid = windowSize between 1 and 100.
  - If invalid: error TRUE, status 16#8200; preserve average/windowSizeReached. No history change. Trigger edge history updated to current trigger every scan.
  - If valid: error false status 0.
  - Reset has priority: if valid and reset TRUE, clear history (sampleCount=0, sum=0 perhaps), output avg=0 and reached false. Should also establish last valid window =? Yes "clears history before any same-scan accepted sample"; reset no sample. Need track last valid window. If reset true and valid, likely current can become configured size. Any change? Set lastValidWindowSize = windowSize. Doesn't matter.
  - window changed: if valid and windowSize differs from last valid configured size -> clear history before any same-scan accepted sample. Then sample accepted if not reset and (cyclicExec or triggerRise). Need note window change and reset: reset clears anyway.
  - cyclicExecution accepts exactly one sample per scan and ignores trigger. If both cyclicExecution and trigger rise, one insert only. accept = valid & !reset & (cyclicExecution | triggerRise).
  - triggerRise computed from previousTrigger before update. previousTrigger updated every invocation, including reset/invalid. So trigger edge in invalid scan not accepted, but previousTrigger updated. On next valid scan, if trigger stays true, no rise. Good.
  - windowSizeReached TRUE once accepted sample count reaches windowSize (history length = windowSize), and remains true after full as ring buffer? P5 says windowSizeReached <-> length(historyAfter)=windowSize. Ring buffer history should remain length windowSize when full and after replacements, so remains true. If window size changes valid, clears then fills. Reset false.
  - Moving average over active window; after full, discard oldest.
  - average mean of actual samples, no zero fill. When empty 0.

Need incorporate LREAL; sum accumulation can cause drift. Fixed tolerance 1e-5 relative on T2? Need robust. Could recompute sum from array on each sample for precision, but values maybe large? Assumption finite, LREAL doubles. Recompute from active history gives mean with <= n rounding. A running sum with subtraction may drift on sequences. Better recompute arithmetic mean directly each accepted sample by looping over history count. Or maintain sum and subtract but precision issues. Since max 100, recompute each accept is safe. Formal verifier may model? Verify tool likely knows ST->SMV supports bounded? Formal verification against LTL perhaps model can use simpler arithmetic? LREAL maybe unsupported. Need try.

