    history[writeIndex] := value; writeIndex := (writeIndex + 1) MOD 100 (or if >= windowSize then 0, because after clearing write index tracks 0..windowSize-1; when changing window, clear. Thus wrapping at windowSize works: writeIndex := writeIndex + 1; IF writeIndex >= windowSize THEN writeIndex := 0; END_IF. But if windowSize? valid 1..100. For historyCount < windowSize, increment.
