- On reset or window change: historyCount := 0; writeIndex := 0; maybe clear array? Not necessary; mean only count. But initial pre-scan outputs zeros. For formal ghost, history cleared. Could clear array loop, but unnecessary and cost. However when window changes and same scan accept, old entries remain beyond new count but not used. If later window changes larger, we clear. Fine.
- On invalid preserve average/reached and history. On valid after invalid, error/status cleared; window may be changed? last valid retained. If invalid window was e.g. 0, lastValidWindowSize remains previous. Returning to valid same previous value -> no clear; preserve history? Assumption says "An invalid-window scan preserves average/windowSizeReached. Returning to a valid window clears error/status." It doesn't explicitly say history preserved or cleared. Atomic proposition history: "historyAfter after clearing on reset/window change and adding one accepted sample". "windowChanged current valid windowSize differs from last valid configured size". Invalid scans do not update last valid configured size. If returning to same size, no window change, and history could be preserved. But is history preserved across invalid scans? Invalid window does not accept/change history. So yes preserve. If new valid different from last valid, clear. Good.
